A||||10||LAMBO||Looking to buy '87 coupe, doesn't run||||1||
Z||000000||LAMBO||06-21-2001||12:06 PM||||I'm looking at possibly buying a non-running 87 coupe. A salvage yard picked it up from someone that said he was going down the road when it just quit. No pops, bangs or unusual noises, just quit. The salvage yard guy thinks timing gear, which is good for me as a negotiating factor. What could be other options that are less drastic to fix. The car is in otherwise very good condition. Thats why they haven't salvaged the title yet. Should I save this car? It's an auto with AC and 103K miles.<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||06-21-2001||01:22 PM||||I'd say have him crank it over and watch the rocker arms through the oil filler hole.  If they move, it's not the timing gear!<P>It could be the DIS brick (the module that the coilpaks mount to).  This part is surprisingly expensive ($85 at AutoZone).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||06-21-2001||02:45 PM||||What are they asking for it?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||LAMBO||06-21-2001||04:10 PM||||Hasn't got that far yet, Songman. I'm going back to look at it more thoroughly in the next day or two. I'm thinking they gave $50 to $75 tops for it. Maybe they'll take a couple hundred for it. They also have a pretty decent black 87 sc in good running conditon. Needs a couple of interior fixes. It'll probably take $900 to $1000 to get it bought. It does have a clear title.<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||06-21-2001||04:56 PM||||seems pretty odd that they would get a good car that only needs a motor, and they would let it go for a couple hundred?<P> couldnt they swap a motor into it and get at lest 10 bills?<P> isnt that what wrecking yards are for?<P> or look at it this way - if the car is complete except for the block, then they are sitting on several hundred dollars worth the pulled parts - bumpers, body panels, headlight motors, ECM, glass, seats...<P>  doesnt add up.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||06-21-2001||05:02 PM||||Okay.. the reason I am asking is that I have my near perfect <B>88</B> coupe for sale for $1000 that only needs a cam gear. For that you get the 88 suspension, all the new parts that I have put on it, and a CD player...<P>Yes.. I'm trying to sell my car! heheh<BR>I got projects sitting here that I need the cash for...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon7.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||AkursedX||06-21-2001||05:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>Okay.. the reason I am asking is that I have my near perfect [b]88</B> coupe for sale for $1000 that only needs a cam gear. For that you get the 88 suspension, all the new parts that I have put on it, and a CD player...<P>Yes.. I'm trying to sell my car! heheh<BR>I got projects sitting here that I need the cash for...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon7.gif">  <P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I wish you were a little closer to me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||LAMBO||06-21-2001||05:14 PM||||Ken,<BR>I've bought from these guys before. If they can turn a couple hundred dollars on something in a short turnaround, they'll do it. Fiero parts aren't a real hot commodity in this part of the country, so there better off selling a good condition, non-running one to someone (like me). The time, parts cost and labor it would take them to get the car up and running could never be recouped. That black coupe I mentioned earlier sat out in front of their place on a busy highway for almost a year, and no one bought it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||06-21-2001||08:11 PM||||Check the valve motion as described above. After that... check for spark, fuel, etc... Be carefull on spark... DIS is allot hotter than regular ignition.<P>Even if the motor is fried... you can get new motors for it for cheap enough. From Olds Cutlass Calias or Grand Am. Same motor. just swap pulleys and brackets. (Get e new belt tensioner... Those are not worth saving.) You might be able to talk them into a motor and car package. Odds are good they have at least one that runs good.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Hartz||06-21-2001||08:32 PM||||Engine swap!  Engine Swap!  Engine Swap!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||12
